  speakerName: VENDOR IRAH
  speakerPortrait: {fileID: 0}
  dialogueText: 'Welcome, traveler!

    When someone helps you, gives you something,
    or does something kind for you, it is important to show appreciation.

    In
    Ilokano, ''agyamanak'' means ''thank you.''

    You can use it whenever you
    want to express gratitude.

    Listen carefully: agyamanak.

    Now, try saying
    ''agyamanak'' yourself."

'
